Compilation flags:
========================================
Enable : MODEL=HYDRO, TURBULENCE
Disable: COMOVING, PARTICLE, GRAVITY
Default optional: MHD, FLU_SCHEME=MHM_RP, EOS=ISOTHERMAL

Default setup:
========================================
1. Code units:
   (1) Dimensionless OPT__UNIT=0
   (2) Magnetic field is scaled to MagZ=Turb_B0/UNIT_B -> initial magnetic energy density = 0.5*Turb_B0^2/(4*pi)
   (3) Adjust MOLECULAR_WEIGHT and ISO_TEMP so Cs=1

2. BOX_SIZE         1
   NX0_TOT_X        64
   NX0_TOT_Y        64
   NX0_TOT_Z        64

3. MAX_LEVEL        0
   OPT__BC_FLU_*    1  (periodic)

4. END_T            default to 100 code unit

5. Turbulence parameters:
   SRC_TURBULENCE        1    enable turbulence
   SRC_TURB_VEL          0.2  target velocity dispersion in code unit
   SRC_TURB_KDRIV        2.0  driving scale, this will affect Ornstein-Uhlenbeck auto-correlation time (turnover time): Tdecay = BOX_SIZE/(SRC_TURB_VEL*SRC_TURB_KDRIV)
   SRC_TURB_KMIN         1.0  minimum wave number in units of 2*pi/BOX_SIZE
   SRC_TURB_KMAX         3.0  maximum wave number in units of 2*pi/BOX_SIZE
   SRC_TURB_ZETA         1.0  fully solenoidal
   SRC_TURB_SPEC_FORM    1    parabolic spectrum
   SRC_TURB_UPDATE_STEP  10   number of turbulence driving pattern updates per turnover time, so dt for OU process = Tdecay/SRC_TURB_UPDATE_STEP
   SRC_TURB_TABLE_SIZE   128  resolution of turbulence table, must be a power of 2. The actual table size is (SRC_TURB_TABLE_SIZE + 1)^3

Optional:
   (1) Increase MAX_LEVEL
   (2) Turn on OPT__FLAG_VORTICITY as refinement criteria.
   (3) Adjust thresholds in Input__Flag_Vorticity

Alternatively with other fluid scheme and equation of state:
   (1) FLU_SCHEME=MHM, need to set DT__FLUID=0.3 in Input__Parameter, default -1 will be reset to 0.4 which is unstable for this test.
   (2) EOS=GAMMA, set GAMMA=1.01 in Input__Parameter
   (3) FLU_SCHEME=CTU, requires EOS=GAMMA

Note:
   DT__FLUID=0.4 for MHM shows unphysical results for default settings, one way to avoid this is to increase driving force.
   To increase forcing without changing much target velocity, increase SRC_TURB_KDRIV.

Reference:
========================================
1. Turbulence Generator: paper:       Federrath et al. (2010), A&A 512, A81 (https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/200912437)
                         source code: TurbGen (https://github.com/chfeder/turbulence_generator)

2. Test problem inspired by Pakmor et al. (2026) (arXiv:2607.06660)

